Q: What is best practice for preventing a class attribute from becoming stale data? A: <p>You can label the fields you want to have behavior on setting, or be computed on getting, as <a href="https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#property" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>@property</code></a>.</p>
<p>One way to do this is to compute your internal set property when it's first accessed (that is, lazily).</p>
<pre class="lang-py prettyprint-override"><code>class AlphabetString:
  def __init__(self, istr: str):
    self._string = istr
    self._alphabet: frozenset[str] | None = None

  @property
  def alphabet(self) -&gt; frozenset[str]:
    if self._alphabet is None:
      self._alphabet = frozenset(self._string)
    return self._alphabet

  @property
  def string(self) -&gt; str:
    return self._string

  @string.setter
  def string(self, istr: str) -&gt; None:
    self._string = istr
    self._alphabet = None
</code></pre>
<p>Now if <code>astr = AlphabetString(&quot;foo&quot;)</code>, you can access <code>astr.alphabet</code> and get the frozenset containing <code>f</code> and <code>o</code>, and it will be cached if you access it again.  But if you reassign <code>astr.string = &quot;bar&quot;</code> and then access <code>astr.alphabet</code> again it will be recomputed.  You're not allowed to try to assign <code>astr.alphabet = frozenset()</code> since that doesn't have a setter.</p>
<p>You also have the choice of computing the alphabet <em>eagerly</em>, in the constructor and in the string setter function.  This simplifies the typing a little bit (the internal <code>self._alphabet</code> is never None) but it could waste some cycles if you're never looking up the value.</p>

Q: How can I make an infinite-scrolling marquee? I can&#39;t get my items to repeat A: <p>Here's my attempt:</p>
<ul>
<li>Create a copy of the &quot;strip&quot; and place the 2 strips side by side (using flex).</li>
<li>Translate both divs to the left until the right end of first div goes off the screen.</li>
<li>At this point, the front part of the second div fully covers the screen, making it indistinguishable from the initial state.</li>
<li>Then loop over the animation.</li>
</ul>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="true" data-babel-preset-react="true" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const arr = ['AAA','BBB','CCC','DDD','EEE','FFF','GGG','HHH','III','JJJ','KKK','LLL','MMM','NNN','OOO','PPP','QQQ','RRR','SSS','TTT','UUU','VVV','WWW','XXX','YYY','ZZZ']


function App() {

  return (
    &lt;div className='w-auto my-5'&gt;
          &lt;div className='overflow-hidden d-flex'&gt;
              {/* 2 copies */}
                {[1, 2].map((i) =&gt; (
          &lt;div className='animate-marquee d-flex' key={i}&gt;
                      {arr.map((text, j) =&gt; (
                          &lt;div className='px-3' key={j}&gt;{text}&lt;/div&gt;
                        ))}
                    &lt;/div&gt;
                ))}
            &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
  )
}


ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById("root")).render(&lt;App/&gt;)</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>@keyframes marquee {
  to {
    transform: translateX(-100%);
    }
}

.animate-marquee {
  animation: marquee 10s linear infinite;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div id="root"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.2.0-beta1/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet"/&gt;
&lt;script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/react/18.3.1/umd/react.production.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/react-dom/18.3.1/umd/react-dom.production.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>You can further enhance with pause on hover and masking with a linear gradient.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="true" data-console="true" data-babel="true" data-babel-preset-react="true" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code snippet-currently-hidden">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const arr = ['AAA','BBB','CCC','DDD','EEE','FFF','GGG','HHH','III','JJJ','KKK','LLL','MMM','NNN','OOO','PPP','QQQ','RRR','SSS','TTT','UUU','VVV','WWW','XXX','YYY','ZZZ',]


function App() {

  return (
    &lt;div className='w-auto my-5 mx-2' style={{
                mask: 'linear-gradient(to right, transparent, black 20%, black 80%, transparent 100%)'
            }}&gt;
          &lt;div className='overflow-hidden d-flex'&gt;
              {/* 2 copies */}
                {[1, 2].map((i) =&gt; (
          &lt;div className='animate-marquee d-flex' key={i}&gt;
                      {arr.map((text, j) =&gt; (
                          &lt;div className='px-3' key={j}&gt;{text}&lt;/div&gt;
                        ))}
                    &lt;/div&gt;
                ))}
            &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
  )
}


ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById("root")).render(&lt;App/&gt;)</code></pre>
